  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "To locate a square root, look for perfect squares on either side of the number. Here,\n\\[\n12^2=144<164<169=13^2.\n\\]\nAmong positive numbers, a larger number has a larger square. Therefore the positive number whose square is \\(164\\) lies between \\(12\\) and \\(13\\). The answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
